WEBVTT

00:01.960 --> 00:04.130
As Helck continues to win his way
through the tournament,

00:04.130 --> 00:06.250
Vermilio tries to thwart him with traps.

00:06.460 --> 00:10.460
However, Helck makes it through all of them
and clinches a spot in the finals.

00:11.040 --> 00:14.420
Another member of the Four Elite Lords,
Azudra the Blue,

00:14.420 --> 00:17.880
suggests that the final challenge of the tournament
should be retaking Castle Urum

00:17.880 --> 00:20.500
by defeating the winged soldiers
that have invaded it.

00:20.960 --> 00:25.880
<b>The Road to Castle Urum</b>

00:20.960 --> 00:25.880
<b>Castle Urum</b>

00:20.960 --> 00:25.880
<b>Underground Path</b>

00:20.960 --> 00:25.880
<b>Rest Areas</b>

00:20.960 --> 00:25.880
<b>Tournament Arena</b>

00:21.210 --> 00:23.750
And so, Vermilio ends up accompanying Helck

00:23.750 --> 00:25.920
and the other competitors there.

00:51.420 --> 00:53.670
A crazed cog in the machine

00:53.670 --> 00:56.330
Lets loose a shrill cry

00:56.330 --> 00:58.330
Destined for battle and foaming at the mouth

00:58.330 --> 01:01.170
As if waiting for an opening

01:01.420 --> 01:03.540
I got dealt a dangerous card

01:03.540 --> 01:06.170
But prediciments are opportunities

01:06.170 --> 01:08.080
There's no way in hell I'm giving up

01:08.080 --> 01:10.960
The last one standing is the winner

01:11.170 --> 01:13.330
Let's just dance hand in hand

01:13.330 --> 01:16.080
With the grinning devil

01:16.080 --> 01:18.330
No need to care about appearances

01:18.330 --> 01:20.670
Courage trembles with fury

01:20.670 --> 01:23.630
Before the darkness can consume it all

01:23.830 --> 01:24.500
Break it

01:24.500 --> 01:26.000
Kick it away

01:26.000 --> 01:29.080
It's your common sense that'll be smashed to bits

01:29.080 --> 01:33.580
Ignite a flame in the soul that no one can extinguish

01:33.880 --> 01:39.290
This prayer that I now offer to the endless world

01:39.290 --> 01:44.080
Will never stop until the day comes when it gets answered

01:44.080 --> 01:45.710
Always burning

01:45.710 --> 01:48.580
It's my soul

01:56.040 --> 02:00.960
<b>The Unknown Enemy</b>

02:07.420 --> 02:09.460
Feels nice out here.

02:09.960 --> 02:12.790
So this is the land where humans reside.

02:12.790 --> 02:16.420
I've never been this far inside
of their territory before.

02:16.420 --> 02:17.710
It's incredible.

02:17.710 --> 02:20.710
Nothing at all like the
decayed wastelands of the Empire.

02:21.710 --> 02:24.960
Which makes sense given that our lands
are overflowing with an invisible toxin.

02:24.960 --> 02:28.330
Just staying outside for too long
can get us killed.

02:28.500 --> 02:31.330
That's why all of our major hubs,
like the castles and cities,

02:31.330 --> 02:35.040
are always covered in a barrier
that keeps us safe from the toxin.

02:36.040 --> 02:39.710
But I guess they don't need anything like that here.

02:39.710 --> 02:43.790
And it doesn't take any hard work
for them to maintain this environment, either.

02:43.960 --> 02:48.130
I can't deny I'm a little envious
of the humans that get to live here.

02:48.540 --> 02:50.250
Well, I should get a move on.

02:50.250 --> 02:52.630
Just need to head southwest
and I'll reach the royal capital.

02:52.790 --> 02:54.920
It's the enemy stronghold...

02:54.920 --> 02:57.830
Have to be careful
not to get caught or I'm screwed.

02:58.630 --> 03:02.000
Oh yeah, I heard that as part
of the finals for the tournament,

03:02.000 --> 03:05.290
Lady Vermilio had to leave on an expedition
to Castle Urum with that one hero.

03:05.290 --> 03:09.880
I can't give this mission any less than my best
knowing that she's out there working even harder.

03:10.170 --> 03:11.580
Okay! Just stay calm!

03:11.580 --> 03:13.830
Everything will work out even if
I have to go to some extremes!

03:15.670 --> 03:18.500
For the peace of the Empire! Let's do this!

03:26.670 --> 03:27.420
Awesome.

03:27.420 --> 03:28.420
Most impressive!

03:28.960 --> 03:31.040
She's taking this a little too far.

03:31.040 --> 03:33.540
Hey, be careful not to go overboard.

03:33.540 --> 03:34.380
Yes, ma'am.

03:34.380 --> 03:35.710
Uh, "ma'am"?

03:39.290 --> 03:41.460
It seems like the number of monsters
has increased again.

03:41.750 --> 03:44.040
I just hope one of those doesn't show up...

03:44.040 --> 03:46.330
I must say, those are some
strange-looking bugs.

03:46.330 --> 03:47.330
Well, yeah,

03:47.330 --> 03:50.920
that's because they're monster bugs that
were created by the toxin plaguing this land.

03:51.460 --> 03:53.540
A toxin, you say?

03:53.540 --> 03:54.960
There are so many of these things!

03:54.960 --> 03:57.880
And we still have a long ways to go
until we reach a rest area!

03:58.040 --> 03:59.670
I wish they'd give us a break already.

03:59.830 --> 04:02.830
Then perhaps it would be best
if I handled this situation.

04:02.830 --> 04:05.420
I can take care of all the monsters at once.

04:05.420 --> 04:07.460
Hmm. What a good opportunity.

04:07.460 --> 04:10.880
Since this guy made it to the finals,
I'd like to see exactly what he's capable of.

04:14.790 --> 04:15.710
He's eating a snack?!

04:15.710 --> 04:17.040
And what good is that supposed to do?

04:17.500 --> 04:20.290
He must be getting ready to use
a type-2 special ability.

04:20.290 --> 04:21.380
Indeed.

04:21.380 --> 04:23.040
By eating some beans,

04:23.040 --> 04:26.290
I become capable of generating
an extremely durable barrier.

04:26.290 --> 04:27.920
Okay, but you're eating chocolate!

04:27.920 --> 04:29.080
Oh drat!

04:29.080 --> 04:31.170
I have such a sweet tooth
I just couldn't help it!

04:32.170 --> 04:32.880
No worries!

04:33.540 --> 04:34.750
Choco-holic!

04:34.750 --> 04:36.880
Neither of you has an anxious bone
in your damn body, do you?

04:36.880 --> 04:37.580
Come on!

04:37.580 --> 04:39.630
If you're gonna put a barrier,
then do it fast!

04:39.630 --> 04:41.130
Their numbers are just growing!

04:41.130 --> 04:42.130
Very well.

04:42.130 --> 04:44.250
I shall show you the full extent of my powers.

04:49.630 --> 04:51.420
Now that's a crazy amount of power!

04:51.420 --> 04:52.670
How amazing!

04:52.670 --> 04:55.500
Does he really have to do
all that groaning for it to work?

04:58.880 --> 05:00.080
Oh jeez, now there's more of them!

05:00.080 --> 05:00.830
Hey!

05:00.830 --> 05:02.790
Just how long does it take
for your barrier to activate?!

05:02.790 --> 05:04.210
Well...

05:04.210 --> 05:06.460
about 30 minutes or so, I'd say.

05:07.130 --> 05:08.830
We'll all be bug food by then!

05:08.830 --> 05:10.170
YOU FOOL!

05:11.080 --> 05:12.330
Whoa! Awesome!

05:12.330 --> 05:13.330
Most impressive!

05:14.080 --> 05:15.540
I knew it...

05:25.420 --> 05:27.540
That must one of the rest areas, eh?

05:27.880 --> 05:29.540
I know it doesn't look very big,

05:29.540 --> 05:32.830
but there's a barrier around the place
to keep us safe from the toxin.

05:37.130 --> 05:39.330
Whew! I'm bushed!

05:39.330 --> 05:40.920
Seriously, just exhausted.

05:40.920 --> 05:41.920
Shut up.

05:42.250 --> 05:46.080
We went a whole day without any breaks
to make it here after leaving the stadium.

05:46.670 --> 05:49.000
So I suppose it's only natural
for all of them to be tired.

05:52.000 --> 05:53.750
All except for one, that is...

05:53.750 --> 05:55.790
Oh shoot! I accidentally broke it!

05:55.790 --> 05:57.880
Bummer! You're in trouble now!

05:58.420 --> 06:00.250
Hand it to me, if you please.

06:00.250 --> 06:02.630
Restoration magic is one of my specialities.

06:02.630 --> 06:03.580
Sorry, and thanks!

06:03.790 --> 06:07.040
He hasn't shown any signs of exhaustion
at all this entire time.

06:08.170 --> 06:12.210
I had been wondering how exactly he made
the long journey to reach the stadium...

06:12.210 --> 06:13.380
And now I understand.

06:13.380 --> 06:15.380
His stamina must be practically infinite.

06:15.380 --> 06:18.460
It's still unclear to me if he has
high resistance to the toxin or not,

06:18.460 --> 06:23.630
but it seems safe to say that obstacles
of this level don't even pose a challenge to him.

06:24.960 --> 06:25.920
Splendid!

06:25.920 --> 06:27.830
Nice! Let's have something to eat now!

06:27.960 --> 06:31.420
The power of Helck the hero... is mighty indeed.

06:34.290 --> 06:35.330
By the way...

06:35.830 --> 06:36.880
What is it?

06:37.080 --> 06:40.420
Is that Anne girl actually
some kind of big shot or what?

06:40.420 --> 06:42.210
I noticed you were being really formal with her.

06:42.210 --> 06:43.380
Seriously?

06:43.380 --> 06:45.460
You better watch your attitude around her.

06:45.460 --> 06:46.960
Okay, so she is a big shot.

06:49.710 --> 06:50.880
Listen here.

06:50.880 --> 06:53.330
You have to promise not to freak out.

06:53.330 --> 06:54.250
Uh, sure.

06:54.250 --> 06:56.750
This is just a hunch,
but I'm pretty sure she's actually...

06:56.750 --> 06:59.080
Lady Vermilio of the Four Elite Lords.

06:59.080 --> 07:01.080
Huh? Like for real?

07:01.330 --> 07:04.830
What kind of reaction is that?
Show a little surprise, dammit!

07:04.830 --> 07:07.500
Come on, you literally just told me
not to freak out.

07:07.710 --> 07:09.710
But what's Lady Vermilio doing here?

07:09.710 --> 07:12.960
That should be obvious!
She's keeping tabs on Helck!

07:12.960 --> 07:13.790
What for?

07:13.790 --> 07:15.130
How stupid can you get?

07:15.130 --> 07:18.750
She's obviously taking precautions
because he's a hero from the human realm!

07:18.750 --> 07:20.210
But Helck's a stand-up guy!

07:20.210 --> 07:21.460
Like that matters.

07:21.960 --> 07:23.670
In any case, Lady Vermilio-

07:23.670 --> 07:26.000
I mean, Ms. Anne deserves our respect,
so you better-

07:27.420 --> 07:29.170
You seem to have the wrong idea.

07:29.170 --> 07:31.710
I'm just Anne from management
and nothing more.

07:31.710 --> 07:34.540
So don't you dare go around
calling me an "Elite Lord."

07:34.540 --> 07:37.040
Especially not in front of the big guy.

07:37.540 --> 07:38.670
Big guy?

07:39.250 --> 07:40.250
Are we clear?

07:40.250 --> 07:42.420
I'm only part of the management staff.

07:42.420 --> 07:45.000
Don't get all humble.
Treat me like anybody else.

07:45.290 --> 07:46.210
Sure!

07:46.580 --> 07:48.000
Uh, yes, ma'am.

07:49.080 --> 07:51.830
Oh! I mean, no problem...

07:52.670 --> 07:53.830
That's more like it.

07:53.830 --> 07:55.750
But do NOT start calling me any nicknames.

07:55.750 --> 07:56.920
I hate those.

07:58.080 --> 08:00.290
Well shucks! Guess you were wrong!

08:02.080 --> 08:03.750
Here! Thanks for waiting!

08:04.290 --> 08:05.830
Eat up while it's still hot!

08:05.830 --> 08:07.670
Whoa! This looks tasty!

08:10.290 --> 08:11.670
I love the cheese!

08:11.670 --> 08:15.290
I wasn't expecting to eat
Helck's cooking a second time!

08:15.580 --> 08:17.710
Hey, guys, feel free to take it easy!

08:17.710 --> 08:19.500
I'll fix us something to eat!

08:19.500 --> 08:23.210
We already have instant food on hand,
but this guy just keeps showing off at every turn!

08:23.540 --> 08:25.880
And why the hell
did he put eggplants in here?!

08:25.880 --> 08:28.580
Eggplants are one of the foods I can't stand!

08:29.750 --> 08:33.750
It seems Lady Vermilio is being extra wary
about eating any of Helck's cooking.

08:33.750 --> 08:36.040
Uh oh. Did I make something you don't like?

08:38.790 --> 08:40.420
I'm just going to have to eat it.

08:40.420 --> 08:43.500
Otherwise, he might get the impression
that I suspect him of something.

08:43.500 --> 08:46.830
Plus I need to keep him convinced
that I'm only a member of the management staff.

08:46.830 --> 08:48.540
No, everything's fine.

08:48.540 --> 08:49.540
I'll eat it.

08:50.330 --> 08:53.040
Gah! Curse you for this, Helck!

08:53.040 --> 08:55.040
I swear I'll have my revenge someday!

08:56.250 --> 08:57.540
Oh...

08:57.540 --> 08:59.000
It's good.

09:01.460 --> 09:03.880
One, two, three, four, five.

09:03.880 --> 09:05.500
That's the end, I win.

09:06.250 --> 09:07.960
How could I lose again?!

09:09.080 --> 09:11.500
You're just too easy to beat, Lord Azudra.

09:11.500 --> 09:13.210
Also, you're bleeding.

09:13.210 --> 09:14.380
Lord Azudra!

09:14.380 --> 09:16.540
I have a report on the status of the competitors!

09:16.540 --> 09:18.170
Sure. Go ahead.

09:19.210 --> 09:23.250
Our tournament finalists have departed
from the second rest area.

09:23.580 --> 09:27.000
However, since it seems there is a fierce storm
on the planned route ahead,

09:27.000 --> 09:30.380
they'll be heading to Castle Urum
by taking the underground path instead.

09:30.630 --> 09:31.880
Hmm.

09:31.880 --> 09:34.880
Well, seeing as how Vermikins is with them,
it should be all right.

09:34.880 --> 09:37.670
Is there anything of concern
in that underground path?

09:37.830 --> 09:42.130
The toxin down there is especially potent
and spawns a very high volume of monsters.

09:42.130 --> 09:44.630
It doesn't matter how many you wipe out,
since they always come back right away,

09:44.630 --> 09:47.580
which is why we've reluctantly
had to abandon use of that path.

09:49.290 --> 09:50.040
Enough!

09:50.040 --> 09:51.750
There's no point in worrying her like that!

09:51.750 --> 09:53.170
Oh! I'm so sorry!

09:53.170 --> 09:54.130
No more food for you, Hon.

09:54.130 --> 09:55.830
Huh?! For how long?!

09:56.000 --> 09:56.830
O-oh gosh.

09:56.830 --> 09:58.790
You know, it really wasn't that big of a deal...

09:59.290 --> 10:03.790
It's just that we've had so many
ominous things happening around here lately.

10:03.790 --> 10:06.040
I honestly can't help but feel concerned.

10:06.040 --> 10:09.250
I mean, just imagine if something
were to befall Lady Vermilio...

10:10.710 --> 10:12.790
It's not too late to change plans.

10:12.790 --> 10:15.540
Don't you think we should organize
some troops and send them to serve as escorts?

10:16.000 --> 10:17.540
I understand how you feel,

10:17.540 --> 10:20.710
but Vermikins makes the best use of her powers
when there are less people around.

10:21.040 --> 10:25.920
Sending troops on an escort mission after them
would very likely just end up getting in her way.

10:25.920 --> 10:27.040
YOU FOOL!

10:27.040 --> 10:29.290
Yeah... wide area attacks are her thing.

10:29.290 --> 10:30.500
Not to mention,

10:30.500 --> 10:32.960
there is still a decent chance
those winged knights

10:32.960 --> 10:34.920
will launch a surprise attack on us here,

10:34.920 --> 10:36.830
so cutting down the size of our forces is risky.

10:37.000 --> 10:38.670
Y-you make a good point.

10:38.670 --> 10:40.250
I'm sorry for bringing it up.

10:40.250 --> 10:42.540
It's fine, you don't need to worry.

10:42.750 --> 10:45.080
Vermikins is incredibly strong.

10:45.080 --> 10:48.540
So much so that all of us together
wouldn't even compare in terms of sheer power.

10:49.420 --> 10:50.500
Right!

10:50.500 --> 10:51.380
That's enough of that!

10:51.380 --> 10:53.880
Come and play a game
to get things off your mind, Ms. Ista!

10:53.880 --> 10:56.290
Lord Azudra is so easy to beat it's laughable!

10:56.290 --> 10:58.290
O-oh, no, I couldn't...

10:58.710 --> 11:00.420
Despite everything I said,

11:01.290 --> 11:03.460
I'm actually quite concerned myself.

11:03.460 --> 11:04.830
Please, Vermikins.

11:04.830 --> 11:07.630
You gotta get back here safe and sound!

11:15.790 --> 11:17.580
The toxin is very potent here.

11:17.580 --> 11:20.040
Don't bother fighting any monsters
other than the ones directly in our way!

11:20.500 --> 11:21.670
Okay!

11:24.130 --> 11:26.130
There are so many varieties of monsters!

11:26.130 --> 11:27.330
Pretty incredible, huh?

11:27.330 --> 11:29.130
And all of them are super ferocious!

11:29.130 --> 11:30.380
Let me give you the lowdown!

11:30.380 --> 11:31.880
This one's a plant type!

11:31.880 --> 11:33.960
Watch out for their acid, it's a major pain!

11:33.960 --> 11:35.540
Over here is a beast type!

11:35.540 --> 11:37.630
Be careful not to get hit by their claws or horns!

11:37.630 --> 11:39.750
And they always jump around,
which is a major pain!

11:39.920 --> 11:44.460
Next up, we've got a reptile type.
Guess what? They're a major pain!

11:44.630 --> 11:46.420
I'm learning so much!

11:46.630 --> 11:47.830
Check out this one!

11:47.830 --> 11:49.420
Oh wait, it's just another beast type.

11:49.710 --> 11:51.880
What do you keep getting so excited about?

11:51.880 --> 11:52.670
Hey!

11:52.670 --> 11:55.130
Would it kill you guys to be
a little more on edge about this?

11:55.130 --> 11:56.500
Okay, so this one here...

11:56.500 --> 11:57.330
Uh-huh!

11:58.130 --> 11:59.330
Have you lost your minds?!

11:59.330 --> 12:01.040
The monsters are gonna surround us again!

12:01.040 --> 12:04.000
Goodness me. What a helpless bunch.

12:04.330 --> 12:05.250
Very well.

12:05.250 --> 12:08.330
This seems like a good chance
for me to use my super durable barrie-

12:08.330 --> 12:10.580
We don't have 30 minutes to wait, dammit!

12:10.580 --> 12:13.500
Ver- I mean Lady Anne... er, Ms. Anne!

12:13.500 --> 12:15.380
Oh jeez, just use whatever name you want!

12:15.380 --> 12:16.210
What is it?!

12:16.210 --> 12:17.670
Lady Anne, behind you!

12:23.000 --> 12:25.420
Look at those dark markings! And it's size!

12:25.420 --> 12:26.460
Preposterous.

12:26.460 --> 12:28.420
There's no doubt about it! That's gotta be...

12:28.670 --> 12:32.330
Just what I was hoping to avoid.
A New-World Lifeform!

12:38.460 --> 12:40.420
New-World Lifeforms.

12:40.630 --> 12:43.170
These appear from time to time
in areas with high toxin levels.

12:43.170 --> 12:46.580
And although similar in appearance,
they have a different nature from regular monsters.

12:47.380 --> 12:51.380
They attack everything indiscriminately,
whether it be people or monsters,

12:51.380 --> 12:54.880
and grow to become even more vicious
as a result of their constant battles.

12:54.880 --> 12:56.630
I'll exterminate this one myself!

12:56.630 --> 12:58.040
The rest of you should stay bac-

12:58.500 --> 13:00.460
I'm very familiar with these...

13:01.670 --> 13:02.750
Interesting.

13:02.750 --> 13:06.130
So this was yet another monster that
the toxin of this land has created, eh?

13:06.250 --> 13:07.330
What?!

13:07.330 --> 13:09.210
I get the impression
he's going to try and fight it alone...

13:09.210 --> 13:10.710
For real? That's nuts!

13:10.880 --> 13:12.540
It shouldn't be much an of issue.

13:12.540 --> 13:13.630
Look closely.

13:13.630 --> 13:15.710
Helck has a weapon
hanging from his left hip.

13:15.960 --> 13:16.790
A sword?

13:17.670 --> 13:19.880
Helck was already
ridiculously strong barehanded,

13:19.880 --> 13:21.880
so just imagine him swinging that sword.

13:22.170 --> 13:23.210
Oh yeah.

13:23.210 --> 13:25.830
Now that I think about it,
he only used his fists in the tournament.

13:41.790 --> 13:42.790
He kicked it!

13:42.790 --> 13:44.290
Seriously, just a kick?

13:44.290 --> 13:45.250
That's a kick all right.

13:45.380 --> 13:47.500
It's not over yet, you simpletons!

13:53.880 --> 13:54.540
Victory!

13:54.540 --> 13:55.460
So dinky!

13:55.880 --> 13:57.830
How about that?! Feast your eyes!

13:57.830 --> 13:59.460
Oh please, don't even.

13:59.460 --> 14:01.830
He clearly picked
the wrong time to draw his sword!

14:01.830 --> 14:03.790
That's the shortest sword I've seen!

14:03.960 --> 14:06.880
Anyway, seems like he really did
beat it with that attack.

14:06.880 --> 14:08.170
What's his deal?

14:08.170 --> 14:09.750
That's Helck for you!

14:09.750 --> 14:10.750
Take a look!

14:10.750 --> 14:12.380
The path has been cleared for us!

14:12.380 --> 14:13.670
Okay! Let's run for it!

14:14.420 --> 14:16.420
Lady Ver- I mean, Lady Anne?

14:16.420 --> 14:18.000
Oh, sorry.

14:19.040 --> 14:20.330
You can go on ahead.

14:20.580 --> 14:23.830
I'm going to burn its corpse,
just to be extra safe.

14:24.080 --> 14:25.210
Nice work!

14:25.210 --> 14:26.920
You're really something else, dude!

14:26.920 --> 14:28.380
But your sword is so dinky!

14:28.380 --> 14:31.000
That was very impressive.
I shall give you some chocolate.

14:31.000 --> 14:32.170
Thanks!

14:32.380 --> 14:34.330
Yeah, I can't deny that was incredible.

14:34.330 --> 14:37.040
I'm not so confident about my chances
of winning the finals now.

14:38.330 --> 14:39.330
Helck...

14:39.330 --> 14:41.330
Based on what he said earlier,

14:41.330 --> 14:43.880
he must have known
about the New-World Lifeforms.

14:47.500 --> 14:50.170
Does that mean they appear
in the human realm, too?

14:50.580 --> 14:54.210
But I thought our efforts to keep
the toxin from spreading were working...

14:55.580 --> 14:56.580
Dammit.

14:56.580 --> 14:59.630
New mysteries just keep piling up one by one.

14:59.630 --> 15:01.580
What the hell is going on?

15:05.000 --> 15:06.170
Hoo boy!

15:06.170 --> 15:07.750
We finally made it!

15:08.250 --> 15:09.500
There's Castle Urum!

15:13.710 --> 15:16.250
<b>Spy Level: 43</b>

15:13.710 --> 15:16.250
<b>Intelligence Operative: Kushiki</b>

15:14.830 --> 15:16.290
I've been awaiting your arrival.

15:16.290 --> 15:18.040
Whoa! That's badass!

15:20.960 --> 15:22.250
Here we are.

15:22.460 --> 15:23.460
This is it.

15:24.330 --> 15:25.670
Isn't that just a rock?

15:25.670 --> 15:27.630
Reciting the proper incantation here

15:27.630 --> 15:30.540
will turn this into a hidden passage
that leads right into Castle Urum.

15:30.540 --> 15:31.790
Wow.

15:32.080 --> 15:34.170
Pardon! May I come in?

15:39.540 --> 15:41.790
I've done everything that I can for you.

15:42.040 --> 15:44.250
Good luck. And please be careful out there.

15:44.250 --> 15:46.920
Of course. You've done excellent work, soldier.

15:46.920 --> 15:48.710
Your praise is more than I deserve.

15:49.080 --> 15:51.540
You two are totally letting the facade slip...

15:51.540 --> 15:52.750
Goodbye!

15:55.040 --> 15:57.460
After we pass through here,
you'll go straight into battle.

15:57.710 --> 15:59.000
And just as a reminder,

15:59.000 --> 16:01.460
whoever among you
takes down the enemy leader

16:01.460 --> 16:03.420
shall be crowned the
victor of the tournament.

16:03.830 --> 16:06.710
So if you want to be Demon Lord,
then defeat the leader.

16:06.710 --> 16:08.880
However, do not push your limits.

16:08.880 --> 16:10.960
If you get in over your head,
then run away immediately.

16:10.960 --> 16:12.790
I will cover you and handle the rest.

16:12.790 --> 16:13.580
Right!

16:13.580 --> 16:14.540
Yes, ma'am!

16:14.710 --> 16:15.920
The time has come.

16:15.920 --> 16:18.500
I have to admit, I'm getting a little nervous...

16:18.500 --> 16:20.710
Know what? I bet you're totally gonna win!

16:20.710 --> 16:21.960
I mean, you're super strong!

16:21.960 --> 16:24.000
Gosh! You think so?

16:24.750 --> 16:27.500
I ran out of chocolate. I wanna go home.

16:27.750 --> 16:30.210
Why do these two seem so unmotivated?

16:30.210 --> 16:30.920
No, wait.

16:30.920 --> 16:32.580
Kenros is practically a master of speed,

16:32.580 --> 16:35.040
so he must have his eye on zipping in
to land the final blow.

16:35.380 --> 16:37.920
And since Dorsche can use
a type-2 special ability,

16:37.920 --> 16:40.750
it's very possible he has
what it takes to defeat the enemy.

16:40.960 --> 16:44.130
They're putting on this lazy act
to try and throw us off.

16:44.130 --> 16:47.630
But I know their type and they're
always obsessed with winning in the end.

16:47.630 --> 16:49.330
I'm not letting my guard down.

16:49.540 --> 16:52.130
Man, it'd be awesome if Helck
became the new Demon Lord!

16:52.380 --> 16:54.670
He's such a stand-up guy.
I'm gonna throw my weight behind him!

16:55.380 --> 16:58.420
All I care about is making sure
that Lord Urum is avenged.

16:58.420 --> 17:01.170
Let's hurry and get this over with
so I can go home and eat chocolate!

17:02.000 --> 17:05.170
That said, Helck is still the one
I need to be the most wary of!

17:05.790 --> 17:09.250
Because I know that damn hero
is way stronger than I am...

17:09.460 --> 17:11.710
So there's only one way
I can pull off the win.

17:11.710 --> 17:15.380
And that's to defeat the enemy leader
before he even has a chance to make his move.

17:15.670 --> 17:17.960
I'm not letting you win this, you friggin' hero!

17:19.830 --> 17:23.170
I am the one responsible for
informing Helck about the tournament.

17:24.330 --> 17:25.460
I figured as much.

17:25.460 --> 17:27.960
Oh? So you already knew?

17:28.170 --> 17:30.790
As I was listening to you
explain your idea for the finals,

17:30.790 --> 17:33.130
I started to have an inkling that was the case.

17:33.630 --> 17:38.380
After all, the place you were found laying
gravely injured was just outside of Castle Thor.

17:39.080 --> 17:41.960
So I'm betting that's where
you met with Helck, right?

17:41.960 --> 17:43.130
Bingo.

17:43.130 --> 17:44.880
Yes, for you see...

17:45.460 --> 17:48.750
that was the day I finished doing everything
necessary to create the Deep Green Contract.

17:48.750 --> 17:52.000
And it left me will some time to kill,
which is why I paid a visit to Castle Thor.

17:54.830 --> 17:57.000
I knew from a single glance...

17:57.210 --> 17:59.330
that he would be trouble.

17:59.880 --> 18:01.540
Helck was incredibly strong.

18:01.830 --> 18:04.750
He fell into numerous traps that I laid out for him,

18:04.750 --> 18:07.330
but he didn't seem to take
even a lick of damage from them.

18:07.670 --> 18:09.960
I honestly thought I was going to die.

18:09.960 --> 18:11.170
It makes sense.

18:11.460 --> 18:13.580
Even though you were stripped of your powers,

18:13.580 --> 18:17.000
I was positive that no ordinary human
or monster would be enough to take you down.

18:17.880 --> 18:21.170
So you suffered those wounds
in battle against Helck, I take it?

18:21.170 --> 18:23.130
No. I didn't.

18:23.130 --> 18:24.040
Huh?

18:24.960 --> 18:28.130
These are all wounds that I got
from one of my own traps.

18:28.460 --> 18:32.380
I miscalculated and then walked
straight into a trap that I had set up.

18:33.330 --> 18:34.460
A careless blunder.

18:34.460 --> 18:36.170
You've gotta be kidding me.

18:36.420 --> 18:38.380
That was just the start of my problems.

18:38.380 --> 18:40.920
The floor gave out and caused me to fall.

18:40.920 --> 18:43.250
And then I landed in a horde of vicious monsters.

18:43.250 --> 18:45.540
Which is when a sandstorm suddenly kicked up...

18:45.920 --> 18:48.420
By the time I regained consciousness,
I was lying in bed.

18:48.420 --> 18:50.250
I'm impressed you made it out alive.

18:50.250 --> 18:51.630
No kidding.

18:51.880 --> 18:53.380
But throughout all of that,

18:53.380 --> 18:56.580
if Helck had shown
even a little of his full power...

18:57.170 --> 19:00.170
I would have undoubtedly lost my life.

19:04.380 --> 19:07.380
After that experience,
it's a safe bet that Azudra trusts Helck.

19:07.380 --> 19:08.290
Whoosh!

19:08.290 --> 19:10.920
It's true that Helck is different than
any other human we've encountered.

19:10.920 --> 19:14.170
However, I'm not sure that's
reason enough for us to trust him.

19:14.170 --> 19:17.290
I just can't shake the feeling
that some part of him is lying to us.

19:17.790 --> 19:20.080
Dammit! This is so annoying!

19:21.290 --> 19:22.630
Heave-ho.

19:24.880 --> 19:27.500
It's all clear. No enemies here.

19:30.000 --> 19:30.830
Oh man!

19:30.830 --> 19:32.250
I'm starting to feel like a nervous wreck!

19:32.250 --> 19:34.080
Fool! Keep your voice down!

19:34.080 --> 19:35.170
Good grief.

19:35.170 --> 19:36.920
You really are slow on the uptake, Kenros.

19:36.920 --> 19:38.790
So are you! Duck down and hide your head!

19:39.710 --> 19:40.750
Well now.

19:42.210 --> 19:43.580
There they are.

19:43.830 --> 19:45.540
And that one must be the leader.

19:45.710 --> 19:48.580
Hmm. I'm only seeing seven enemies here.

19:48.580 --> 19:49.670
There aren't any others around.

19:49.670 --> 19:51.330
This might be our big chance.

19:51.330 --> 19:53.380
They're gonna notice, dammit!
Learn to spy better!

19:53.380 --> 19:54.460
Oh, my apologies.

19:54.460 --> 19:55.750
They've already noticed us.

19:55.750 --> 19:57.080
AW HELL! YOU FOOL!

19:57.080 --> 19:58.210
START THE BATTLE!

19:58.210 --> 19:59.000
Sweet!

19:59.000 --> 20:01.170
I'm going to leave
the bigger ones for you guys.

20:01.170 --> 20:02.960
Just let me handle the leader.

20:02.960 --> 20:05.000
Hold up, did you forget the rules
of the tournament?

20:05.170 --> 20:06.130
Hmph!

20:06.290 --> 20:07.460
That wasn't much of an answer.

20:07.710 --> 20:09.670
Well, whatever!
Time to get out there and do my thing!

20:09.670 --> 20:12.920
Once we've avenged Lord Urum,
I'm going straight back home!

20:13.170 --> 20:14.580
Give me a break.

20:14.580 --> 20:17.960
Who just rushes in like that
without getting a grasp on the situation first?

20:19.210 --> 20:21.210
They're still lacking in so many ways.

20:28.420 --> 20:31.080
Will you really fight, Helck?

20:34.880 --> 20:35.960
You better.

20:39.790 --> 20:41.630
Slowpokes! Slowpokes!

20:41.630 --> 20:43.380
You can't hit me with attacks like that!

20:43.380 --> 20:45.580
But since I don't have a weapon,
I can't beat you either!

20:47.080 --> 20:48.130
Protection!

20:48.580 --> 20:49.500
They're pretty tough.

20:49.500 --> 20:52.460
Just what you'd expect from soldiers
who took down a Demon Lord.

20:52.790 --> 20:54.330
Their leader is still so far away.

20:54.330 --> 20:55.710
I need to hurry!

21:19.830 --> 21:22.630
I promise you

21:22.630 --> 21:25.580
Someday when the world

21:25.580 --> 21:27.670
Comes to an end

21:27.670 --> 21:30.290
I hope we meet once again

21:42.380 --> 21:47.750
Someone once told me

21:47.750 --> 21:53.670
You were like a flower

21:53.670 --> 21:59.210
In a room without water, yet surely

21:59.210 --> 22:01.710
Blooming towards tomorrow

22:03.420 --> 22:06.210
If it was all a dream

22:06.210 --> 22:09.080
To know you

22:09.080 --> 22:12.000
To be in love

22:12.000 --> 22:15.500
I wouldn't know the meaning of life

22:16.330 --> 22:19.130
Even if tomorrow

22:19.130 --> 22:21.830
The rain pours

22:21.830 --> 22:24.210
Dawn will come and

22:24.210 --> 22:27.290
Rainbows will arch over the world

22:27.670 --> 22:30.380
The pain in my heart

22:30.380 --> 22:33.250
The tears trickling down

22:33.250 --> 22:36.710
Let's turn it into seeds for the future

22:36.710 --> 22:38.330
We go on

22:39.040 --> 22:41.080
Until our clumsy love

22:41.080 --> 22:44.250
Blooms into a flower

22:46.040 --> 22:50.830
<b>Next Episode</b>

22:46.040 --> 22:50.830
<b>Shock</b>

22:46.790 --> 22:49.250
Next time: "Shock"
